Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes. It infers and reversibly removes predictable numeric columns, stores reconstruction metadata in the compressed file, and compresses with bz2, with a general-purpose fallback. The corpus compresses from 313,972 to 4,609 bytes: 98.532% size reduction, versus 35,399 bytes for default zlib. Both CLI commands passed a byte-for-byte comparison, additional round-trip tests passed, and python3 assay.py prints the verified reduction score.